@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il28-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-s48-area-order`
IMPORT `ito-s48a-foreign-worker-regs`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Row IL-28: which instrument governs a taxpayer's credit points, and what the
-- credit points are in place of ss 34, 36, 36A and 37 of the Ordinance.
--
-- A person the Area order reaches, or the foreign worker Regulations reach, does
-- not get the points the ordinary sections give; rows IL-01 (ss 34, 36, 36A),
-- IL-02 (s 66) and IL-08 (s 37 and the rest) refuse such a person by name and
-- this module is what answers in their place. A person neither instrument
-- reaches is not answered here: the ordinary sections govern.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Row IL-28 — the credit points of a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen, or of a foreign worker`

§§ `The readings`

-- Every fork at its default: a refusal by name where the text does not decide.
@ref Meng's ruling SHRUG, 2026-10-08
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
`the readings this row takes` MEANS
    `The readings of the forks of row IL-28` WITH
        `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                    IS `declined where residence decides section 36A`
        `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion` IS `declined where income from personal exertion decides section 36`
        `fork F4, residence in the Area for part of a tax year` IS `declined for residence in part of a tax year`
        `fork FW1, the cited sections' conditions`              IS `declined where the cited sections' residence conditions decide`
        `fork FW2, the tax years from 2002 to 2014`             IS `declined for the tax years from 2002 to 2014`
        `fork FW3, regulation 3(d) and deductions`              IS `declined where regulation 3(d) and the chapter's deductions meet`
        `fork OV, both instruments reach the taxpayer`          IS `declined where the order and the regulations both reach the taxpayer`

-- The most generous reading of each fork, for the tests that keep the other readings by name.
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
`the readings that give the most` MEANS
    `The readings of the forks of row IL-28` WITH
        `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                    IS `section 36A has no residence condition`
        `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion` IS `section 36 for every individual`
        `fork F4, residence in the Area for part of a tax year` IS `one residence status for the whole tax year`
        `fork FW1, the cited sections' conditions`              IS `the regulations give their points without the cited sections' residence conditions`
        `fork FW2, the tax years from 2002 to 2014`             IS `no instrument under section 48A applied before the regulations of 5775-2014`
        `fork FW3, regulation 3(d) and deductions`              IS `regulation 3(d) reaches credits only, which is all the power of section 48A gives`
        `fork OV, both instruments reach the taxpayer`          IS `the Area order prevails`

-- The most restrictive.
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
`the readings that give the least` MEANS
    `The readings of the forks of row IL-28` WITH
        `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                    IS `section 36A gives its half point only to an Israeli resident`
        `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion` IS `section 36 only for an individual with income from personal exertion`
        `fork F4, residence in the Area for part of a tax year` IS `apportioned by the months of residence, as section 41 apportions`
        `fork FW1, the cited sections' conditions`              IS `the cited sections' own residence conditions still apply`
        `fork FW2, the tax years from 2002 to 2014`             IS `no instrument under section 48A applied before the regulations of 5775-2014`
        `fork FW3, regulation 3(d) and deductions`              IS `regulation 3(d) reaches the whole chapter as it is written`
        `fork OV, both instruments reach the taxpayer`          IS `the foreign worker regulations prevail`

§§ `Which instrument reaches the taxpayer`

@ref ITO s 48 line 1807; s 48A line 1811; ORD s 1; REG 1, 3(d), 4; fork OV
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`both the Area order and the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, and the sources do not say which prevails` MEANS
    REFUSE "both the Area order and the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, and the sources do not say which prevails"

-- A resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen and who is also a foreign worker within the Regulations (a
-- worker whose stay or employment needs a visa under the Entry into Israel Law) is reached by the Order, which applies
-- ss 34, 36 and 37 to him, and by reg 3(d), which takes the chapter's provisions from him but a few points. The Order is
-- of 1995 and the Regulations of 2014; neither says which prevails (fork OV).
@ref ITO s 48 line 1807; s 48A line 1811; ORD s 1; REG 3(d); fork OV
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A `Which instrument reaches the taxpayer`
`the instrument that reaches` t `, under` r MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the Regulations reach the taxpayer as a foreign worker` t
               THEN IF `the Order reaches the taxpayer` t
                    THEN `the Area order reaches the taxpayer`
                    ELSE `neither instrument reaches the taxpayer`
           IF NOT `the Regulations govern the tax year of` t `, under` r
               THEN IF `the Order reaches the taxpayer` t
                    THEN `the Area order reaches the taxpayer`
                    ELSE `neither instrument reaches the taxpayer`
           IF NOT `the Order reaches the taxpayer` t
               THEN `the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER r's `fork OV, both instruments reach the taxpayer`
               WHEN `the foreign worker regulations prevail` THEN `the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer`
               WHEN `the Area order prevails` THEN `the Area order reaches the taxpayer`
               WHEN `declined where the order and the regulations both reach the taxpayer`
                   THEN `both the Area order and the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, and the sources do not say which prevails`

@ref ITO s 48 and s 48A
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`neither the Area order nor the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, so the ordinary sections govern and are not decided here` MEANS
    REFUSE "neither the Area order nor the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, so the ordinary sections govern and are not decided here"

§§ `The credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37`

@ref ITO s 48 and s 48A; ORD s 1; REG 3
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A `Credit points`
`the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER `the instrument that reaches` t `, under` r
    WHEN `neither instrument reaches the taxpayer`
        THEN `neither the Area order nor the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, so the ordinary sections govern and are not decided here`
    WHEN `the Area order reaches the taxpayer` THEN `the credit points the Order gives to` t `, under` r
    WHEN `the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer` THEN `the credit points the Regulations give to` t `, under` r

@ref ITO s 34; ORD s 1; REG 3
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points under section 34 in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r MEANS
    (`the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r)'s `the points under section 34`

@ref ITO s 36; ORD s 1; REG 3
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points under section 36 in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r MEANS
    (`the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r)'s `the points under section 36`

@ref ITO s 36A; ORD s 1; REG 3
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points under section 36A in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r MEANS
    (`the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r)'s `the points under section 36A`

@ref ITO s 37; ORD s 1; REG 3
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points under section 37 in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r MEANS
    (`the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r)'s `the points under section 37`

GIVEN c IS A `Credit points`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total of` c MEANS
      c's `the points under section 34`
    + c's `the points under section 36`
    + c's `the points under section 36A`
    + c's `the points under section 37`

@ref ITO s 33A (the value of a credit point is an input: row IL-03, s 120B)
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r MEANS
    `the total of` (`the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r)

-- Section 37's text is held only from the tax year 2023 (ito-s48-area-order.l4), so for 2017 to 2022 the total above
-- refuses for an Area resident. The three sections that do not depend on it can still be asked for.
@ref ITO ss 34, 36, 36A; ORD s 1; REG 3(a) to (c)
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A alone in place of the ordinary sections for` t `, under` r MEANS
      (`the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r)'s `the points under section 34`
    + (`the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r)'s `the points under section 36`
    + (`the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r)'s `the points under section 36A`

-- The credit is the points times the value of one point for the tax year, which s 120B indexes (row IL-03) and which this
-- row takes as an input with no default. This is the credit BEFORE it is set off against the tax: s 33A sets it off
-- against the tax of the year, and the result cannot go below zero (row IL-01, fork F5).
@export The amount in NIS of the credit points that Income Tax Ordinance ss 48 and 48A, with the Area order of 5755-1995 and the foreign worker Regulations of 5775-2014, give in place of ss 34, 36, 36A and 37 to a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen or to a foreign worker, before set-off against the tax, given the value of one credit point for the tax year; refuses where neither instrument reaches the taxpayer, where the text of a tax year is not held, and by name where the sources do not decide (forks F1, F2, F4, FW1, FW2, FW3, OV, Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08)
@ref ITO s 33A, s 48, s 48A
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
      `the value of one credit point for the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r `, at` `the value of one credit point for the tax year` MEANS
    `the total credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r TIMES `the value of one credit point for the tax year`

§§ `What the instrument does to each provision of Chapter Three`

@ref ITO s 48 and s 48A; ORD s 1; REG 3(d)
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
      p IS A `A provision of Chapter Three`
GIVETH A `What an instrument does to a provision`
`what the instrument that reaches` t `, under` r `, does to` p MEANS
    CONSIDER `the instrument that reaches` t `, under` r
    WHEN `neither instrument reaches the taxpayer`
        THEN `neither the Area order nor the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, so the ordinary sections govern and are not decided here`
    WHEN `the Area order reaches the taxpayer` THEN `what the Order does to` p
    WHEN `the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer` THEN `what the Regulations do to` p `, under` r
